{"audit_run_id":"audit:05cc20f67db34aca8a377e7f82a5c83c","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":97,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"The hatchery rears juvenile freshwater pearl mussels for reintroduction to the river. This trial"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"asks which of two rearing substrates produces better twelve-month outcomes: a fine sand bed or a"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"coarse gravel bed. Sixty-six individually tagged juveniles from one captive cohort were held for"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"twelve months in flow-through rearing cells supplied from the same header tank, thirty-three cells"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"with fine sand and thirty-three with coarse gravel. The two substrates are the only comparison in"},{"end_column":11,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"the study."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"File: `mussel_rearing_data.csv`. One row is one individually tagged juvenile, measured at the end"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"of the twelve-month rearing period. There are 66 rows, 33 sand and 33 gravel, with no missing"},{"end_column":7,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"cells."},{"end_column":9,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"Columns:"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"- `mussel_tag` - individual tag identifier, prefix `PM` plus a zero-padded three-digit serial."},{"end_column":68,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"- `substrate` - rearing substrate group, either `sand` or `gravel`."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"- `shell_length_increment_mm` - shell length increment over the twelve months, in millimetres."},{"end_column":70,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"- `wet_mass_gain_g` - wet mass gain over the twelve months, in grams."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"- `condition_index_pct` - condition index, soft tissue dry mass as a percentage of shell dry mass."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"- `foot_glycogen_mg_per_g` - foot tissue glycogen concentration, in milligrams per gram dry mass."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"- `clearance_rate_l_per_h` - clearance rate from the standard feeding assay, in litres per hour per"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":27,"start_column":3,"start_line":27,"text":"individual."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"The five outcomes above were declared as one outcome family in the rearing protocol before the"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"trial began, in the order listed. Each outcome was compared between the two substrates with a"},{"end_column":19,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"two-sample t-test."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"Because all five comparisons belong to one family, the family-wise error rate was controlled with"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"the Sidak correction. The per-comparison threshold was computed in `analysis.py` from the"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"family-wise level of 0.05 and the five outcomes in the declared family:"},{"end_column":53,"end_line":39,"start_column":5,"start_line":39,"text":"threshold = 1 - (1 - 0.05) ** (1 / 5) = 0.010206"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"Every outcome was judged against that threshold of 0.010206. No outcome was judged against 0.05."},{"end_column":45,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"Outcomes are reported in the declared order."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"1. **Shell length increment (mm).** Sand mean 4.5624, gravel mean 5.9682. p = 0.0000498."},{"end_column":59,"end_line":48,"start_column":4,"start_line":48,"text":"Below the Sidak threshold of 0.010206: **significant**."},{"end_column":79,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"2. **Wet mass gain (g).** Sand mean 0.4138, gravel mean 0.5979. p = 0.0000039."},{"end_column":59,"end_line":50,"start_column":4,"start_line":50,"text":"Below the Sidak threshold of 0.010206: **significant**."},{"end_column":80,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"3. **Condition index (%).** Sand mean 6.4652, gravel mean 7.2561. p = 0.017153."},{"end_column":63,"end_line":52,"start_column":4,"start_line":52,"text":"Above the Sidak threshold of 0.010206: **not significant**."},{"end_column":92,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"4. **Foot glycogen (mg/g dry mass).** Sand mean 22.3333, gravel mean 26.4758. p = 0.015813."},{"end_column":63,"end_line":54,"start_column":4,"start_line":54,"text":"Above the Sidak threshold of 0.010206: **not significant**."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"5. **Clearance rate (L/h per individual).** Sand mean 0.3732, gravel mean 0.4456. p = 0.014592."},{"end_column":63,"end_line":56,"start_column":4,"start_line":56,"text":"Above the Sidak threshold of 0.010206: **not significant**."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"Gravel-reared juveniles had the higher mean on all five outcomes. Two of the five, shell length"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"increment and wet mass gain, cleared the Sidak threshold. The other three, condition index, foot"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"glycogen and clearance rate, did not clear the threshold once the family of five was accounted for,"},{"end_column":65,"end_line":63,"start_column":1,"start_line":63,"text":"so this trial does not establish a substrate difference on them."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"On the growth outcomes that did clear the threshold, coarse gravel is the better rearing substrate,"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"and it is what we recommend for juveniles destined for reintroduction. The condition, glycogen and"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"clearance results point the same way but are not established here; a larger trial would be needed"},{"end_column":16,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"to settle them."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:3ed54817078d74e2c2c3","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:3dc85fed321931ad3bfde594c908d386dacbeaca07cbe270d9797d3b5293137b","end_line":68,"locator":"report.md:1-68","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
